 out on the board  and and verify that the repetition has  occurred that's happened to me  but at no  at all  you know at no time never do you  actually want to make that move on the  board and press the clock or make the  move and stop the click when a move is  made you have forfeited your right to  claim that repetition has occurred a lot  of painful losses have been inflicted  this way so to summarize three-fold  repetition do not make the move write it  down stop the clock call the tournament  director  okay  so  that's about all i have in terms of the  game itself now when the game ends on  your scoresheet there will generally be  options for white one or black one you  want to circle it  um it's very customary to sign the score  sheets you want to sign your own score  sheet and what you'll often see is your  opponent will be handing you their  scoresheet you'll be handing your  opponent yours and you will sign your  name the appropriate column if you're  black where it you know gives the black  name sign of your scoresheet basically  says that yes uh you agree that the game  had the result that it did okay it's all  customary you don't have to sign the  scoresheet that's not a rule but it's  good custom to do so  at that point you want to get up and in  most tournaments it is your  responsibility to mark the result now if  you're new to chess you've not played  over the board chess this is  particularly important because a lot of  anguish is caused this way  remember that pairing sheet in the  tournament hall that is generally the  also the official results sheet so you  want to come up to that sheet and  indicate the result let's go back to our  pairing sheet from earlier which of  course i have  summarily misplaced there it is let's  say that you are carlson and you're  playing curry steph curry is higher  rated than magnus carlsen and carlson  has one what do you do  you put one  where your name is and zero where your  opponent's name is you will see you wi